From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:04:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linux-dmabuf: accept scan-out-only dmabufs without
 direct-display

A dmabuf the renderer cannot import is refused unless the client marked
it with weston_direct_display_v1. Generic clients (GStreamer, mpv) do not
know that Weston protocol, so a buffer that a KMS plane could show, but
the GPU cannot sample (Allwinner video engine tiled NV12 with lima),
never gets displayed.

If the renderer import fails but the backend can scan the buffer out,
accept it as a direct-display buffer: it is only shown on a plane, and
the renderer draws the usual placeholder otherwise.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 libweston/linux-dmabuf.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c b/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c
index d37121d..45609f3 100644
--- a/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c
+++ b/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c
@@ -282,8 +282,16 @@ params_create_common(struct wl_client *client,
 		goto avoid_gpu_import;
 	}
 
-	if (!weston_compositor_import_dmabuf(buffer->compositor, buffer))
-		goto err_failed;
+	if (!weston_compositor_import_dmabuf(buffer->compositor, buffer)) {
+		/* The renderer cannot use the buffer, but a plane may be able
+		 * to scan it out (e.g. a format modifier only the display
+		 * engine understands): accept it as a direct-display buffer,
+		 * which is only ever shown on a plane. */
+		if (!weston_compositor_dmabuf_can_scanout(buffer->compositor,
+							  buffer))
+			goto err_failed;
+		buffer->direct_display = true;
+	}
 
 avoid_gpu_import:
 	buffer->buffer_resource = wl_resource_create(client,
-- 
